1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,100
Why doesn't Tokyo flood, even in big typhoons?

2
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:06,600
The secret is hidden 50 m underground.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:11,750
A giant tunnel takes in extra river water and sends it to another river.

4
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:16,500
At the end, there is a huge underground tank, 177 m long.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:21,000
59 pillars, each 18 m tall, hold up the ceiling.

6
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,150
Each pillar weighs 500 tons!

7
00:00:23,150 --> 00:00:28,200
They are this heavy to keep the tank from floating up on groundwater.

8
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:32,750
People call it the 'underground temple'. It keeps Tokyo safe every day.
